4-Month Full-Stack Roadmap
(Compressed & Realistic Version)

Month 1: JavaScript Foundations
Goal: Become comfortable with core JavaScript

Focus:
Variables, functions, arrays, objects
DOM + Events
Asynchronous JavaScript (Promises, async/await)
Fetch API
ES6+ features

Practice:
Build 6–8 small projects
Examples: Todo App, Quiz App, Weather App, Notes App.

Month 2: React
Goal: Build real user interfaces

Focus:
Components, Props, State
Hooks (useState, useEffect, useRef)
Forms & controlled inputs
React Router
API integration

Practice:
Build 4 React projects
Convert previous JS projects into React

Month 3: Backend + Database
Goal: Build working full-stack applications

Focus:
Node.js + Express (or FastAPI if you prefer Python)
REST API (CRUD)
MongoDB or PostgreSQL
JWT Authentication
Connecting React frontend to backend

Practice:
Build 2 full-stack apps (Todo + Notes/Blog)

Month 4: Polish + Deployment + Job Readiness
Goal: Become presentable as a junior developer

Focus:
TypeScript basics
Deployment (Vercel + Render)
Basic Docker
Clean code + GitHub
Security basics
1 polished main project
Resume + LinkedIn + Project explanations
Light DSA practice

Weekly Rhythm:
5–6 days building
1 day revision
Always prioritize projects over passive tutorials

Priority Order:
JavaScript
React
Backend + Database
Deployment + Polish

Key Principle:
Build → Break → Fix → Understand → Repeat
